Since each key is now a **hash** (`HSET key field value`) holding multiple records, the lookup changes from "get the string value of each key" to "get **every field/value** of each matching hash". Here's the adapted model, lookup, writer, and the small ripple effects on handlers.

---

## 1. Model: an entry is now `key + field + value`

```java
/** One record inside a Redis hash: HGET key field → value. */
public record RedisEntry(String key, String field, String value) {

    /** Convenience when values are JSON. */
    public <R> R as(ObjectMapper mapper, Class<R> type) {
        try { return mapper.readValue(value, type); }
        catch (IOException e) { throw new InvalidMessageException("Bad JSON in " + key + "#" + field, e); }
    }

    /** Stable id for idempotency keys / DLT headers. */
    public String id() { return key + "#" + field; }
}
```

```java
public interface NationalCodeLookup {
    /** Every hash record (key, field, value) belonging to this national code. Empty flux = no match. */
    Flux<RedisEntry> findAll(String nationalCode);
}
```

---

## 2. Lookup: find the hash keys, then read all their fields

Two sub-steps, each pluggable:

1. **Which keys?** — `SCAN MATCH *{nc}*` (generic, O(N)) **or** a fixed list of key templates (`customer:{nc}`, `loan:{nc}` → O(1)).
2. **Read the hash** — `HGETALL` (`entries()`) for normal-sized hashes, or `HSCAN` (`scan()`) if a hash can hold thousands of fields.

```java
@Component
@RequiredArgsConstructor
@Slf4j
public class RedisHashNationalCodeLookup implements NationalCodeLookup {

    private final ReactiveStringRedisTemplate redis;
    private final AppProperties props;

    @Override
    public Flux<RedisEntry> findAll(String nc) {
        return resolveKeys(nc)
                .flatMap(this::readHash, props.redis().keyConcurrency())   // HGETALL per key, a few in parallel
                .timeout(props.redis().timeout())
                .doOnError(e -> log.warn("Redis hash lookup failed nationalCode={}", nc, e));
    }

    // ---------- step 1: which keys ----------
    private Flux<String> resolveKeys(String nc) {
        var cfg = props.redis();
        if (cfg.keyTemplates() != null && !cfg.keyTemplates().isEmpty()) {
            // O(1): known key shapes → check existence only
            return Flux.fromIterable(cfg.keyTemplates())
                    .map(t -> t.replace("{nc}", nc))
                    .filterWhen(redis::hasKey);
        }
        // fallback: keyspace scan for keys containing the national code
        var options = ScanOptions.scanOptions()
                .match(cfg.keyPattern().replace("{nc}", escapeGlob(nc)))
                .count(cfg.scanCount())
                .build();
        return redis.scan(options)
                .filterWhen(k -> redis.type(k).map(DataType.HASH::equals));   // ignore non-hash keys
    }

    // ---------- step 2: read all records of one hash ----------
    private Flux<RedisEntry> readHash(String key) {
        ReactiveHashOperations<String, String, String> hash = redis.opsForHash();

        Flux<Map.Entry<String, String>> fields = props.redis().hscan()
                ? hash.scan(key, ScanOptions.scanOptions().count(props.redis().scanCount()).build())  // HSCAN, incremental
                : hash.entries(key);                                                                 // HGETALL, one round-trip

        return fields.map(e -> new RedisEntry(key, e.getKey(), e.getValue()));
    }

    private static String escapeGlob(String s) {
        var sb = new StringBuilder(s.length() + 4);
        for (char c : s.toCharArray()) {
            if (c == '*' || c == '?' || c == '[' || c == ']' || c == '\\') sb.append('\\');
            sb.append(c);
        }
        return sb.toString();
    }
}
```

Config:

```java
public record Redis(
        List<String> keyTemplates,     // preferred: ["customer:{nc}", "loan:{nc}"]
        String keyPattern,             // fallback: "*{nc}*"
        @Min(10) int scanCount,
        @Min(1) int keyConcurrency,
        boolean hscan,                 // true if hashes can be large
        Duration timeout) {}
```

```yaml
app:
  redis:
    key-templates: ["customer:{nc}", "loan:{nc}"]   # remove this list to fall back to SCAN
    key-pattern: "*{nc}*"
    scan-count: 1000
    key-concurrency: 4
    hscan: false
    timeout: 2s
```

### Variant: national code is the **field**, not the key

If instead you write `opsForHash().put("customers", nationalCode, json)` — i.e. one big hash keyed by business, national code as field — the lookup is a direct `HGET` per hash:

```java
@Override
public Flux<RedisEntry> findAll(String nc) {
    return Flux.fromIterable(props.redis().hashKeys())          // ["customers", "loans", "blacklist"]
            .flatMap(key -> redis.<String, String>opsForHash().get(key, nc)
                    .map(v -> new RedisEntry(key, nc, v)), 4);
}
```

And if the field merely *contains* the code (`"0012345678:2024-01"`), use `hash.scan(key, ScanOptions.scanOptions().match("*" + nc + "*").build())` per hash key. Both variants satisfy the same `NationalCodeLookup` interface, so nothing else changes.

