## 3. Writer flow: `RedisWriterHandler` becomes hash-based

```java
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public abstract class RedisHashWriterHandler<T> implements TopicHandler<T> {

    protected final ReactiveStringRedisTemplate redis;

    protected abstract String key(T payload);      // e.g. "customer:" + nationalCode
    protected abstract String field(T payload);    // e.g. recordId / account number
    protected abstract String value(T payload);    // usually JSON
    protected Duration ttl() { return null; }      // null = no expiry

    @Override
    public Mono<Void> handle(T payload, MessageContext ctx) {
        String key = key(payload);
        Mono<Boolean> put = redis.<String, String>opsForHash().put(key, field(payload), value(payload));
        return ttl() == null ? put.then()
                             : put.then(redis.expire(key, ttl())).then();   // TTL is per key, not per field
    }
}
```

`HSET` is naturally idempotent (same field → same value), so this flow needs no extra dedup — a redelivery just rewrites the same record.

---

## 4. Ripple effects on the lookup flow

`NationalCodeLookupHandler`, `EntryFanOut`, and the concrete handlers keep working; only the places that identify an entry should use `id()` (key + field) instead of `key()`:

```java
// concrete handler – one API call per hash record
@Override
protected Mono<Void> onMatchedEntry(LoanRequestEvent p, String nc, RedisEntry e, MessageContext ctx) {
    CustomerRecord rec = e.as(mapper, CustomerRecord.class);
    return api.post("loan-api", "/loans/flag",
            new FlagRequest(p.requestId(), nc, rec),
            Map.of("Idempotency-Key", handlerDedupKey(p, ctx) + ":" + e.id()));   // unique per record
}

// filter on key, field, or value
@Override protected boolean accepts(RedisEntry e) {
    return e.key().startsWith("customer:") && !e.field().startsWith("archived:");
}
```

```java
// PartialFailureException – report which records failed
public List<String> failedIds() { return failed.stream().map(f -> f.entry().id()).toList(); }
// DLT header: x-failed-entries = "customer:0012345678#acc-1,loan:0012345678#L-77"
```

If a handler prefers **one API call per hash key** (all records of a customer in one request) rather than per field, group first:

```java
@Override
protected Mono<Void> onMatch(LoanRequestEvent p, String nc, List<RedisEntry> entries, MessageContext ctx) {
    Map<String, List<RedisEntry>> byKey = entries.stream().collect(groupingBy(RedisEntry::key));
    return Flux.fromIterable(byKey.entrySet())
            .flatMap(kv -> api.post("loan-api", "/loans/flag-batch",
                    new BatchFlagRequest(p.requestId(), nc, kv.getKey(),
                            kv.getValue().stream().map(RedisEntry::value).toList()),
                    Map.of("Idempotency-Key", handlerDedupKey(p, ctx) + ":" + kv.getKey())), entryConcurrency())
            .then();
}
```

